/* feature_actions.def -- single source of truth for menu action -> snake_case names.
 *
 * This is an "X-macro" table: a plain list of data, included more than once with the
 * row macros defined differently each time. The feature layer (features.cpp) and the
 * render bridge (native_bridge.cpp) both build their action-name lookup from THIS list,
 * so the two can never drift apart -- and adding a feature name is a one-line edit here
 * instead of two parallel switch cases that have to be kept in sync by hand.
 *
 *   GTAV_ACTION_NAME(ENUM_SUFFIX, "snake_name")  one action id -> one telemetry name
 *   GTAV_MOD_SLOT_NAME("snake_name")             one entry of the contiguous mod-slot range
 *
 * A consumer defines only the macro it needs and #includes this file; the other macro
 * expands to nothing (the #ifndef guards below supply an empty default). The names map to
 * GTAV_NATIVE_SHELL_ACTION_<ENUM_SUFFIX> in include/gtavmenu/native_bridge.h.
 *
 * The mod-slot pickers (MOD_SPOILER..MOD_HORN) are a contiguous enum range addressed by
 * (action - MOD_SLOT_FIRST), so they are listed once as GTAV_MOD_SLOT_NAME rows and the
 * consumers index an array built from them rather than spelling out 17 switch cases. Keep
 * that block in the SAME order as kVehicleModSlots[] in features/lsc.inc.
 *
 * Not listed here: NONE (0) and the dead SET_TIME_NOON/NIGHT (18/19) placeholders -- they
 * fall through to "none" on purpose (see tests/test_feature_action_names.py).
 */

#ifndef GTAV_ACTION_NAME
#define GTAV_ACTION_NAME(suffix, name)
#endif
#ifndef GTAV_MOD_SLOT_NAME
#define GTAV_MOD_SLOT_NAME(name)
#endif

/* Lifecycle */
GTAV_ACTION_NAME(HIDE, "hide")
